THOUGHT: NullAway still reports `values` as nullable at the dereference, likely because it tracks the original nullable variable rather than the local alias. A more robust fix is to avoid nullable `names`/`values` entirely by creating fresh, non-null arrays per region and using them directly. I’ll change the code so that inside the `else` (region) block, I declare `Array<Object> names = null, values = null;` scoped to each region, and then at the end, if they’re non-null and non-empty, I assign to `region.names`/`region.values`. This removes any cross-region reuse and should make NullAway see that `values` is non-null when used. Then I’ll rebuild and re-grep for the specific error to confirm it’s gone.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && \
sed -i '458,512s/        Page page = null;
        Array<Object> names = null, values = null;/        Page page = null;/' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/graphics/g2d/TextureAtlas.java && \
sed -i '474,512c\          } else {
            Region region = new Region();
            region.page = page;
            region.name = line.trim();
            if (flip) region.flip = true;
            Array<Object> names = null;
            Array<Object> values = null;
            while (true) {
              int count = readEntry(entry, line = reader.readLine());
              if (count == 0) break;
              Field field = regionFields.get(entry[0]);
              if (field != null) field.parse(region);
              else {
                if (names == null) {
                  names = new Array(8);
                  values = new Array(8);
                }
                names.add(entry[0]);
                int[] entryValues = new int[count];
                for (int i = 0; i < count; i++) {
                  try {
                    entryValues[i] = Integer.parseInt(entry[i + 1]);
                  } catch (NumberFormatException ignored) { // Silently ignore non-integer values.
                  }
                }
                values.add(entryValues);
              }
            }
            if (region.originalWidth == 0 && region.originalHeight == 0) {
              region.originalWidth = region.width;
              region.originalHeight = region.height;
            }
            if (names != null && values != null && names.size > 0) {
              region.names = names.toArray(String.class);
              region.values = values.toArray(int[].class);
            }
            regions.add(region);
          }' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/graphics/g2d/TextureAtlas.java && \
./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && \
grep -n "TextureAtlas.java:49[0-9].*dereferenced expression values is @Nullable" new_build_output.log || true
```

